---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, AUTHOR } from '../config';

// EDIT THESE TWO LINES
const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'jouko.aroheina@gmail.com';
const UPDATED = '27 November 2026';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description={`How ${SITE.name} handles visitor data: privacy-friendly statistics without cookies, and what third parties may see.`}>
  <div class="hero-field">
    <header class="page-header wrap">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="dek">What this site measures, what it doesn't, and who to ask.</p>
    </header>
  </div>

  <div class="narrow prose">
    <p>In short: this site uses no cookies, no advertising and no tracking across other websites. It counts page views anonymously to learn which posts are read.</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>The site is run by {AUTHOR.name}. Questions about privacy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>

    <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
    <p>The site uses <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/" rel="noopener">GoatCounter</a>, a privacy-friendly analytics service. It counts page views and gives general information such as which page was viewed, where the visitor came from (referrer), and broad details like country, browser and screen size. It does not set cookies, does not store anything on your device, and does not build profiles of individual visitors or follow them across other sites.</p>
    <p>The purpose is to understand which content is useful and to improve it. The legal basis is a legitimate interest in running and improving the site (GDPR Article 6(1)(f)). Because no cookies or similar identifiers are stored on your device, no consent banner is needed.</p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub receives technical data when your browser requests a page, such as your IP address, and may log it. This is outside my control; see <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</p>

    <h2>YouTube videos</h2>
    <p>Some posts include YouTube videos. Nothing is loaded from YouTube when a page opens. Only when you click play does the video load, from YouTube's privacy-enhanced domain, and from then on Google's own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a> applies to that video. Each video also has a text summary and a plain link, so you can skip the player.</p>

    <h2>Your display preference</h2>
    <p>If you use the Dark/Light switch in the header, your choice is saved in your browser's local storage so the site remembers it. It stays on your device and is never sent to me or anyone else.</p>

    <h2>Fonts and other resources</h2>
    <p>Fonts and images are served from this site itself. No fonts or scripts are loaded from advertising or social media services, and the site has no comments, forms, newsletter or advertising.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right to ask what data is held about you, to have it corrected or deleted, and to object to its processing. Since the statistics are anonymous and cannot be linked back to an individual, there is usually nothing to look up, but you are welcome to ask. You may also complain to your national data protection authority; in Finland this is the <a href="https://tietosuoja.fi/en/home" rel="noopener">Office of the Data Protection Ombudsman</a>.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If the site starts using new tools, this page will be updated first. Last updated: {UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
